DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI DiskForecastPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing loading/empty/error/success
plus the 503 subsystem-unavailable variant over an injectable DiskForecastDataSource seam whose value
types mirror the KMP OperatorConfidence DiskForecastResponse/HypertableSize 1:1 (production binds
OperatorConfidenceStore.diskForecast() through the seam). The page reproduces the web chrome
(title/subtitle), the subsystem-unavailable AlertBanner, the four fleet StatCards (Total / Uncompressed
/ Compressed / Growth, each with its web sublabel, shown only when rows>0), and the hypertables
GlassPanel with an adaptive table — a columnar Grid on macOS/iPad and per-hypertable cards on iPhone —
covering all six web columns plus the severity badge, using the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (no
hand-rolled glass). Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names
(23 keys added); display formatting (formatBytes/fmtNumber/percent) is ported and unit-tested.
Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks (0/0) and an executed model
harness (34/34). The full xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to one pre-existing, out-of-scope
shared-surfaces error (forbidden to commit-fix), with ZERO diagnostics in any of my files.

